##
## Filters for tests that fail only in MSAN builds on Linux
##
## When adding a new filter to this list, please include a short description of
## why the filter is required and create an associated tracking issue.
##

# Upstream Chromium test. Stable upstream (0.2% flake rate over 30 days per
# LUCI Analysis). The recorder panel has heavy initialization (~20 module
# imports, LitElement setup, extension system) that, combined with Brave's
# additional DevTools startup overhead (chromium_src overrides, NTP/stats
# services), exceeds the test's hardcoded 20-second timeout under MSAN
# instrumentation.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/53812
-DevToolsTest.TestShowRecorderTab

# Upstream Chromium test. Stable upstream (0.9% flake rate over 30 days per
# LUCI Analysis). The test performs 10 eval retries with exponentially
# increasing timeouts (total ~10s wall-clock). Combined with Brave's DevTools
# startup overhead (chromium_src overrides, NTP/stats services), this exceeds
# the hardcoded 20-second timeout under MSAN instrumentation. The sibling test
# CantInspectBlockedSubdomainHost is already disabled in the upstream source
# for the same reason.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/54053
-DevToolsExtensionHostsPolicyTest.CantInspectBlockedHost

# Upstream Chromium test. Stable upstream (0.3% flake rate over 30 days per
# LUCI Analysis). The test evaluates a console expression with a
# sourceMappingURL comment and waits for SourceMapWillAttach to fire within a
# hardcoded 20-second JS timeout. Combined with Brave's DevTools startup
# overhead (chromium_src overrides, NTP/stats services), MSAN instrumentation
# causes the DevTools frontend initialization to exceed this timeout.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/53990
-DevToolsTest.SourceMapsFromDevtools

# Upstream Chromium test. Already disabled upstream on ChromeOS MSan
# (crbug.com/491012584). Times out under MSan instrumentation because the
# kInitialWebUI feature (WebUI toolbar) navigation hangs in Brave. Upstream
# flake rate: 2.7% (LUCI Analysis, 30-day lookback).
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/54030
-InitialWebUIMetricsDropBrowserTest.WebiumRendererMetricsDroppedIfNoRule

# Upstream Chromium test. Stable upstream (0.3% flake rate over 30 days per
# LUCI Analysis). Same dangling reference bug as the sibling test above: the
# test captures a const reference to a ServiceWorkerRunningInfo map entry,
# stops the service worker (removing the entry from the map), then passes
# the dangling sw_info.scope to OnStoppedSync(). Caught by MSan as
# use-of-uninitialized-value but does not crash in regular builds.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/55396
-ServiceWorkerStopTrackingBrowserTest.OnStoppedUpdatesBrowserAndRendererState_AfterRenderStopNotification

# Upstream Chromium test. Has failed on every Brave Linux MSan nightly since
# 2026-09-16, while Chromium's Linux MSan bots do not list it as flaky and its
# overall upstream flake rate is below 1%, so the generated filters do not
# cover it. Already disabled upstream on ChromeOS MSan, Windows and macOS
# (crbug.com/491012584).
# The test expects chrome://version to record no samples of
# Webium.Navigation.DocumentLoader.DidCommitNavigation, but
# SubprocessMetricsProvider applies that name to deltas merged from any
# top-chrome WebUI renderer, and HistogramTester takes its baseline without
# merging subprocess deltas. Samples from the browser window's own top-chrome
# WebUI renderers that are not yet merged when the test starts are counted.
# Why Brave's MSan build hits this on every run while Chromium's Linux MSan
# bots do not is not established; there is no local MSan build to reproduce.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/54031
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/59078
-InitialWebUIMetricsMappingBrowserTest.NormalRendererMetricsAreNotMapped
